#{[17592186403584 #edb/ref 1080 "$B$ only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403584 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403584 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "610ceecf-c4a9-5885-8266-6104d4f37cf1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403585 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186403586 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403585 #edb/ref 1069 "q-72492" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403585 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403585 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following matrices are **not** in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403585 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ba6bcd83-87df-5c0b-b121-63a0ff1205ca" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403585 #edb/ref 1074 "Remember that a matrix is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is not in row echelon form since the leading entry ${c}_{22}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated). \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $C$ is **not** in row echelon form." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403586 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403587 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403586 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403588 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403586 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403589 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403586 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403590 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403586 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403591 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403586 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403586 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403586 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186403590 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403586 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "80541a17-4cbb-5d55-a794-14a52b470ccb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403587 #edb/ref 1080 "$A$ and $C$ only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403587 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403587 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d2449f17-fb24-5f21-b93a-91da7cb73b6f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403588 #edb/ref 1080 "$A$ only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403588 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403588 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f82dd2a1-af9f-5176-9521-a602fb86b66c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403589 #edb/ref 1080 "$B$ and $C$ only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403589 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403589 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a73d0fd1-33f8-5fef-91ee-18ea7bc00233" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403590 #edb/ref 1080 "$C$ only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403590 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403590 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1e393d24-d14c-55d4-9c1c-d1fb4487bb44" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403591 #edb/ref 1080 "$B$ only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403591 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403591 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0a24998d-88d6-567d-b060-eecb883f1a8b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403689 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186403690 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403689 #edb/ref 1069 "q-73740" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403689 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403689 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & -10 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403689 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "28d32302-16b0-5cdc-a69e-754fd94318a8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403689 #edb/ref 1074 "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & -10 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+2y=-1 \\\\ 0x+0y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx+2y=-1.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=-1-2y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-1-2y \\\\ y=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1-2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403690 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403691 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403690 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403692 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403690 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403693 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403690 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403694 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403690 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403695 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403690 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403690 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403690 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186403691 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403690 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "0ccee7c5-bc00-583c-adcd-616a8af7768b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403691 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1-2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403691 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403691 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "22cd6aa9-a925-5038-975c-07e44d80e350" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403692 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2+y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403692 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403692 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0e0364cb-677b-524e-aa38-691178112aba" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403693 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1+2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403693 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403693 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6274e549-fa07-5abb-bd6c-53630d47a7b8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403694 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2-y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403694 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403694 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "11509ba5-2bfa-5670-b24e-690396084002" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403695 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1+2y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403695 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403695 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "da9d2dd8-4de7-59f6-8ae5-f0b3a20d355b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403773 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186403774 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403773 #edb/ref 1069 "q-74626" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403773 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403773 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+2y-2z=1 \\\\ -3x-6y+6z=-3 \\\\ 2x+5y=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403773 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "23bca3c5-322d-5c3f-a423-fb871cdd59a3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403773 #edb/ref 1074 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -6 & 6 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ into reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -6 & 6 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the row echelon form above, we have only two pivots (in the $1$st and $2$nd columns). To transform the matrix to reduced row echelon form, we need to create zeros above the pivots only. This gives,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -10 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-10z=-1 \\\\ y+4z=1 \\\\ 0=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final equation, we can remove this equation from the system. \n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=10z-1 \\\\ y=1-4z \\\\ z=z,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}10z-1 \\\\ 1-4z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403774 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403775 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403774 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403776 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403774 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403777 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403774 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403778 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403774 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403779 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403774 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403774 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403774 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186403775 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403774 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "7014ab46-6268-5d03-a678-37850fc6da0a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403775 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}10z-1 \\\\ 1-4z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403775 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403775 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c75e1a37-431f-56e2-b6cd-917ed934bc54" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403776 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}5z-1 \\\\ 1-4z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403776 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403776 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "913376ed-a5cb-5479-ab16-e42eb401612f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403777 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}10z+1 \\\\ 1+4z \\\\ z+1\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403777 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403777 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "082f2000-223e-5c35-8880-3c877b9f58a9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403778 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}10z-1 \\\\ 1-4z \\\\ z+1\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403778 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403778 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c23159c4-b1db-556c-a013-ffc4b8987ced" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403779 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}5z-1 \\\\ 1-2z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403779 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403779 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8545a78e-5e9f-5188-9a89-b26fb6b7b34d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403787 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186403788 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403787 #edb/ref 1069 "q-74634" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403787 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403787 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 2x-y=-1 \\\\  & 2x-4y=3 \\\\  & x+y=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The system is consistent dependent\nII. The system has a unique solution\nIII. The system is inconsistent" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403787 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a8971116-e24d-5808-9b29-a50e168511e5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403787 #edb/ref 1074 "To classify the system, we will first try to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{3}{2} & \\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{9}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y=\\frac{9}{2},$ and it has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, only statement III is true." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403788 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403789 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403788 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403790 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403788 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403791 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403788 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403792 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403788 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403793 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403788 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403788 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403788 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186403791 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403788 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f91e44eb-099d-52c4-a904-f2a31b9b0fa8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403789 #edb/ref 1080 "II and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403789 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186403789 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b9541786-a906-58e9-a152-185ff736eaa6" #edb/ref 17592186